{"id": "EUVD-2026-82168", "enisaUuid": "7c486ee4-2544-3164-87ab-0c0fb07bd241", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/msm: Only fini scheduler after successful init\n\nmsm_ringbuffer_new() destroys a partially initialized ring through\nmsm_ringbuffer_destroy() when an allocation or scheduler setup step\nfails.\n\nIf drm_sched_init() fails before it finishes initializing the scheduler,\nthe failure path still calls drm_sched_fini(). That teardown path assumes\nthe scheduler work items, lists, and workqueue state were initialized.\n\nTrack successful scheduler initialization and call drm_sched_fini() only\nafter drm_sched_init() returned 0.\n\nThis issue was found by a static analysis checker and confirmed by\nmanual source review.\n\nPatchwork: https://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/738905/", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:10:45", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:51:47", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bd2a5a876904eaf688a093cd73986abc3571f26b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aafc9258efeec98fcb7e3998356b4b25bf1ad159", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d43e1bbfd43458b9242806eec77ea3b032134baf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/09b360eb6ce345996a30fad8c86e9df80f41cd7e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e2332abed2a4d3caa59052095dc16e4ce44791ea"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93058", "GHSA-2m9v-9vx7-p7w7"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "012ae017-5562-342b-adbb-0f7c042b6e1e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15"}, {"id": "1b4a6a7b-68f1-36e2-84cf-8243e4fd64a6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "57935fa2-c406-34dd-b246-cabd7692ac96", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "7295ef97-8e0a-31ec-a923-639de565dcd8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1d8a5ca436ee4a28eec14cb813f790f7cdeeee19 <e2332abed2a4d3caa59052095dc16e4ce44791ea"}, {"id": "843932be-f24a-3e1a-b451-8bb2f2b04d09", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "88f18d1e-dda9-3500-9cdb-750a79fa85dd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1d8a5ca436ee4a28eec14cb813f790f7cdeeee19 <aafc9258efeec98fcb7e3998356b4b25bf1ad159"}, {"id": "96178354-8ee1-3cff-ac2f-ccc7a86fd233", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1d8a5ca436ee4a28eec14cb813f790f7cdeeee19 <09b360eb6ce345996a30fad8c86e9df80f41cd7e"}, {"id": "9ec0c3b7-05fa-3881-bb40-e9248e1dd7d1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1d8a5ca436ee4a28eec14cb813f790f7cdeeee19 <bd2a5a876904eaf688a093cd73986abc3571f26b"}, {"id": "b1132e33-b576-3865-9fe9-8fbe0d32a73a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "b2ce25e1-d088-3a6f-89e5-8ca9bc611048", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "bb87ea60-c62e-3f64-b2fd-4f697e738f1d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "bf6da0f0-2dd5-36b1-a3b0-02be31e48d8a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1d8a5ca436ee4a28eec14cb813f790f7cdeeee19 <d43e1bbfd43458b9242806eec77ea3b032134baf"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "89a10e45-3934-33b0-a2d0-e3026ab25127", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}